1
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:58,000
David is 11 years old. He weighs 60 pounds. He is 4 feet, 6 inches
tall. He has brown hair. His love is real. But he is not.

2
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:50,000
A.I. Artificial Intelligence is a drama, science fiction,
adventure film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:42,000
David, a robotic boy—the first of his kind programmed to love—is adopted
as a test case by a Cybertronics employee and his wife.

4
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Though he gradually becomes their child, a series of unexpected
circumstances make this life impossible for David.

5
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:26,000
David, played by Haley Joel Osment.

6
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Gigolo Joe, played by Jude Law.

7
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Monica Swinton, played by Frances O'Connor.

8
00:38:56,000 --> 00:39:02,000
Henry Swinton, played by Sam Robards.

9
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:54,000
Martin Swinton, played by Jake Thomas.

10
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:46,000
Prof. Hobby, played by William Hurt.

11
00:53:32,000 --> 00:53:38,000
Artificial Intelligence (or simply A.I.) is a 2001 science
fiction drama film directed by Steven Spielberg.

12
00:58:24,000 --> 00:58:30,000
The screenplay by Spielberg and screen story by Ian Watson are loosely based on the
1969 short story "Supertoys Last All Summer Long" by Brian Aldiss.

13
01:03:16,000 --> 01:03:22,000
Set in a futuristic society, the film stars Haley Joel Osment as David, a
childlike android uniquely programmed with the ability to love.

14
01:08:08,000 --> 01:08:14,000
Jude Law, Frances O'Connor, Brendan Gleeson and
William Hurt star in supporting roles.

15
01:13:00,000 --> 01:13:06,000
Development of A.I.

16
01:17:52,000 --> 01:17:58,000
originally began after producer and director Stanley Kubrick
acquired the rights to Aldiss's story in the early 1970s.

17
01:22:44,000 --> 01:22:50,000
Kubrick hired a series of writers, including Aldiss, Bob Shaw,
Ian Watson and Sara Maitland, until the mid-1990s.

18
01:27:36,000 --> 01:27:42,000
The film languished in development hell for years, partly because Kubrick felt that computer-generated imagery was not
advanced enough to create the David character, which he believed no child actor would convincingly portray.

19
01:32:28,000 --> 01:32:34,000
In 1995, Kubrick handed A.I.

20
01:37:20,000 --> 01:37:26,000
to Spielberg, but the film did not gain momentum until Kubrick died in 1999.

21
01:42:12,000 --> 01:42:18,000
Spielberg remained close to Watson's treatment for the
screenplay and dedicated the film to Kubrick.

22
01:47:04,000 --> 01:47:10,000
Artificial Intelligence was released on June 29, 2001, by Warner Bros.

23
01:51:56,000 --> 01:52:02,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed
$235.9 million against a budget of $90–100 million.

24
01:56:48,000 --> 01:56:54,000
It was also nominated for Best Visual Effects and Best Original
Score (for John Williams) at the 74th Academy Awards.

25
02:01:40,000 --> 02:01:46,000
In a 2016 BBC poll of 177 critics around the world, A.I.

26
02:06:32,000 --> 02:06:38,000
Artificial Intelligence was voted the eighty-third greatest film since 2000.

27
02:11:24,000 --> 02:11:30,000
It has since been called one of Spielberg's best works and one of the
greatest films of the 21st century, and of all time.

28
02:16:16,000 --> 02:16:22,000
The film explores themes of android, prostitute, artificial
intelligence (a.i.), prophecy, loss of loved one.

29
02:21:08,000 --> 02:21:14,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
